cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If this work helps yours, please cite it as below."
title: "flickering-sign: an autonomous brain in three levels"
abstract: >-
  An autonomous brain packaged as a bundle, in three levels of control: plain code
  that decides each tick whether the moment calls for a choice (with a per-mind Laya
  head distilled at sleep), an LLM read in one pass by its letters' probabilities,
  and the same LLM thinking when an arbiter gives it the floor. Config-declared
  drives and hormones over one event stream, each hormone modelled on its known
  human effects; a hippocampus with sleep consolidation and cues; a cerebellum.
  Several minds live on a small persistent island. Nothing of curiosity or
  cooperation is programmed: the experiment watches what emerges.
type: software
